# This is a sample tab separated file of IMDb tvSeries tconst IDs whose
# episodes should not be expanded.

# When a tvSeries is processed, all its tvEpisodes are also looked up and
# their credits added to the generated spreadsheets. That is how an episode's
# guest cast becomes findable with xrefCast.sh, and for most series it is well
# worth it: a few hundred episodes with a recurring cast and guests who turn
# up in other shows.
#
# The only reason to skip a series is size. A daily soap, a documentary
# anthology like Nova (over 1,000 episodes, almost no recurring people), or a
# parent series like Tatort (over 1,300 episodes) adds thousands of credit rows
# and very few cross-references. Add its tconst below and only its
# series-level credits are kept.
#
# Skipping never changes findOtherShows.sh results -- the cache it reads holds
# series-level credits only.

# Create a similar skipEpisodes file of shows to exclude from episode processing.
# If it has a .skipEpisodes extension, it will be automatically processed.
# However it can have any name and extension and be passed as a parameter
# on the command line using the -s switch, e.g. -s Netflix.skipEpisodes.txt

# Only the tconst field is used. Additional fields are not needed, but useful
# for documentation.
#
# The entries below are for demonstration. Murdoch Mysteries and Silent Witness
# are among the largest expansions in the Contrib files, so skipping them shows
# the effect (generateXrefData.sh -s skipEpisodes.example Contrib/Acorn.tconst),
# but both share enough cast with other shows to be worth keeping in practice.

# tconst	Service	Primary Title	Date
tt1091909	Acorn	Murdoch Mysteries	2008
tt0115355	Britbox	Silent Witness	1996
tt0206501	PBS	Nova	1974
